<http://data.silknow.org/object/22ef26e0-a3a8-39c6-b796-526e4c8d3724>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Textile, sari, woven silk, Bangalore, ca. 1867"@en , "Complete deep yellow silk sari, with fine red checks, one end has a deep yellow and lighter yellow border, with a fine red stripe, the other end has bands of bright pink with stripes of yellow and metal-wrapped thread. The side borders are plain yellow with stripes of white, green and pink."@en , "CHECKED SARI \n\nThis sari incorporates many south Indian characteristics: vivid colours, a checked pattern and a deep pallu (end border). To create the checks and silver bands, extra weft threads were added during weaving. The warp threads were resist-dyed to make the change from yellow to magenta. The intentionally blurred effect where the colour changes is also typical of south Indian weaving.\n\nSilk with silver-wrapped thread\nBengaluru, Karnataka, about 1867\nV&A: 6107 (IS) [03/10/2015-10/01/2016]"@en , "Intended for use as a garment, clothing."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/46330fee-40ac-3012-b61b-5cace5fc3897> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/aedc3969-7c29-3997-b017-5c8c17aa8e54> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/85fd752b-c3d0-39d3-8f05-fbb3765380a3> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/2e7cd9ec-d44d-364d-b5d2-78fd56cd5510> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/f2c9a94f-83aa-3040-b53d-8ff4d5f4ce41> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/01d2bb0d-5bed-363b-b0c7-17f8499ca785> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/1925a2b2-5ebd-3aad-bcc9-fdef82f55805> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/471e9353-7051-3160-8507-218ab78b307d> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e48b7701-9564-3aa8-92dd-ffa76bf559f0> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/f2c8d26c-a961-3da2-b23b-3196ccc4a765> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/ed0391fe-02e2-3237-bf41-2448a599ef62> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/bc00e085-a14e-3a34-bb89-663a7e6395fa> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/f336f5e3-57fb-33f9-8fde-79bf0632debe> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/1520dedf-c176-39b1-ae9b-9b3b16d0490b> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/929b6828-8571-3088-a0b1-b59fd3ad3446> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/a1ec753e-4104-3c6e-8c11-0d36455d6437> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/69da8d11-efb7-3142-ad31-529a921db6fe> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "CHECKED SARI \n\nThis sari incorporates many south Indian characteristics: vivid colours, a checked pattern and a deep pallu (end border). To create the checks and silver bands, extra weft threads were added during weaving. The warp threads were resist-dyed to make the change from yellow to magenta. The intentionally blurred effect where the colour changes is also typical of south Indian weaving.\n\nSilk with silver-wrapped thread\nBengaluru, Karnataka, about 1867\nV&A: 6107 (IS) [03/10/2015-10/01/2016]"@en , "Intended for use as a garment, clothing."@en , "Textile, sari, woven silk, Bangalore, ca. 1867"@en , "Complete deep yellow silk sari, with fine red checks, one end has a deep yellow and lighter yellow border, with a fine red stripe, the other end has bands of bright pink with stripes of yellow and metal-wrapped thread. The side borders are plain yellow with stripes of white, green and pink."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/22ef26e0-a3a8-39c6-b796-526e4c8d3724/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/22ef26e0-a3a8-39c6-b796-526e4c8d3724/dimension/2> ;
